course: dictionary
lesson: 14496
title: A word for a whole group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name one person, and some name a whole group. Peasant means one poor farm worker or small farmer. Peasantry means all the peasants of a country taken together, like a crowd of them in one word. «The peasantry worked the lord's fields from dawn to dusk.» Here the word stands for everyone who worked the land, not just one person.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. The word «lord» tells you the peasantry worked for someone powerful, and «from dawn to dusk» tells you the work was long and hard. Peasantry is a noun with no plural, so you do not say «peasantries» in the usual way. It is a word like «crowd» that names many people together.
explain: The ending -ry often turns a word for one person into a word for a group. Peasant becomes peasantry, and the group is usually a group of people of one kind. When you meet an unknown word ending in -ry, check whether it names a group, and then read the words around it for clues.
fact: Peasantry means all the peasants of a country taken together.
fact: Peasants were poor farm workers and small farmers, especially in the past.
fact: «The peasantry» is a group noun: it names all the peasants at once.
fact: In the Peasants' Revolt of 1381 in England, the peasantry rose up in protest.
fact: In the Holodomor famine of 1932-33 in Ukraine, the peasantry suffered terribly.
exercise: «The peasantry worked the lord's fields from dawn to dusk.» What does peasantry mean? | All the rich lords who owned the land | *All the poor farm workers and small farmers of a country | A group of soldiers guarding a castle | Shops and markets in a busy town
exercise: Which word in «The peasantry paid their lord with grain each autumn» names a group of people? | paid | autumn | *peasantry | grain
exercise: Ella says peasantry is just a fancy word for one farmer. Why is that not quite right? | It means a farmer who is very rich | *It means all the peasants together, a whole group, not one person | It means a farm with animals in it | It means a farmer who lives in a city
test: In 1381 the peasantry in England rose in revolt. What was the Peasants' Revolt? | A war between two kings over a castle | A famine that destroyed all the crops | *A revolt by ordinary poor farm workers and small farmers in England | A royal feast held in the summer
test: «The peasantry suffered terribly in the famine of 1932-33.» Which group does this sentence describe? | The kings of the Middle Ages | The lords of England | *The poor farm workers and small farmers of Ukraine | The soldiers of the Russian Empire
exam: «The peasantry built the castle walls but owned none of the land.» Which word means all the poor farm workers and small farmers together? | built | *peasantry | castle | owned
